Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Iterated Finite Automata", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->856075906,ExpressionUUID->"f32f94f3-1a1f-44b7-b026-48269df07e3c"],

Cell["\<\
An iterated finite automaton applies a finite-state transducer (Mealy \
machine) repeatedly to a row of symbols: each pass reads the row from the \
left, rewriting it while updating the internal state, and iteration produces \
a spacetime evolution analogous to a cellular automaton. Invertible \
transducers generate automata groups \[LongDash] the odometer, the \
lamplighter group and the Grigorchuk group among them \[LongDash] and \
iterated automata probe their dynamics. This paclet follows Andrzej Zuk's \
WSRI26 essay \"Iterated Finite Automata\", supporting explicit transition \
rules, numeric rule codes, and the Mealy and wreath recursion presentations.\
\>", "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->988624525,ExpressionUUID->"87e79b32-fbe5-447c-8f6b-a2f19f7353fe"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

